# tooling caches
/.serena
# Ignore .claude/ contents but keep the design docs in .claude/docs/ tracked.
# All three lines are load-bearing, in this order:
#   1. un-ignore the directory itself — the user's global excludesFile
#      (~/.gitignore_global) ignores `.claude/`, and git will not descend into an
#      excluded directory, so no negation below it can take effect until this
#      repo-level rule (higher precedence) re-admits it;
#   2. ignore the *contents* rather than the directory, because git cannot
#      re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded;
#   3. re-include the design docs, and the shared agent tooling this tree carries to
#      arbitrum-docs on landing: its own .claude/.gitignore, settings.json, hooks/ and agents/.
#
# Skills, hooks and agents are listed one by one on purpose. `.claude/skills/` and
# `.claude/agents/` in a working copy also hold whatever personal skills and agents the developer
# has installed, and a blanket re-include would commit those on the next `git add -A`. Only the
# four arbitrum-docs skills and the one agent below belong in the repo; add another here
# deliberately. `.agents/` (Codex skills) and `.codex/` are tracked wholesale, so they carry no
# rule here; keep personal files out of them.
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/docs/
!/.claude/.gitignore
!/.claude/settings.json
/.claude/agents/*
!/.claude/agents/
!/.claude/agents/diagram-converter.md
/.claude/hooks/*
!/.claude/hooks/
!/.claude/hooks/optimize-svg.sh
!/.claude/hooks/require-pattern-guide.sh
/.claude/skills/*
!/.claude/skills/
!/.claude/skills/arbitrum-brand-svg-diagrams/
!/.claude/skills/arbitrum-brand-video-explainers/
!/.claude/skills/content-audit/
!/.claude/skills/new-doc/
.env*

# PR replay run output
/.pr-replay
